# Inventory Data Cleaning using Microsoft Excel

## Project Overview

This project demonstrates data cleaning and standardization techniques using Microsoft Excel.

The original inventory dataset contained inconsistent text formatting, mixed delimiters, inconsistent capitalization, and unstructured records. The data was transformed into a clean, structured dataset suitable for reporting and analysis.

---

## Objectives

- Clean raw inventory data
- Standardize text values
- Organize data into structured columns
- Improve data quality
- Create analysis-ready datasets

---

## Skills Used

- Microsoft Excel
- Data Cleaning
- Text to Columns
- Excel Functions
- Data Formatting
- Conditional Formatting
- Data Validation

---

## Data Cleaning Performed

- Split raw data into individual columns
- Standardized product names
- Corrected supplier name inconsistencies
- Fixed capitalization issues
- Standardized category values
- Applied professional table formatting
- Created calculated fields:
  - Stock Turnover Ratio (STR)
  - Amount to be Received

---

## Outcome

The dataset was successfully transformed into a structured and analysis-ready format suitable for dashboards, reporting, and business analysis.

